         INFOSYS  2000-C.E.T
1)A bicycle goes 1 mile in three minutes with the wind and returns back  in 
4 min. against the wind.How many minutes he will take to cover 1 mile when
there is no wind?                             (ans-24/7 min)
2)A man passed one sixth of  his life in childhood , one twelfth in youth,
And  one seventh more as a bachelor , 5yrs after his marriage a son was born
Who dies 4yrs before his father at half his final age.What is the total age of
the man ?                                                     (Ans-84)
3)Alpha,Beta Gamma ,Theta and Epsilon.There are 5 different quantities
Are given 
·If and only if alpha=gamma then beta<>epsilon
·Alpha-beta =beta-gamma      alpha>theta
·Alpha>beta  and  gamma>theta
Write the quantities in descending order                          
(Ans – alpha>beta=epsilon>gamma>theta)

4)A thief broke into a jewellery  shop and thought of taking all the diamonds
with him but while he was leaving came to his bitter senses and thought of
taking half with him but he could not resist and took more extra and left .
A second thief came and took half of the remaining and two more .A third thief
came and took half the remaining and two more .Then fourth thief came and did
the same .The fifth thief came and there was no more diamond for him to steal
What was the actual no.of diamonds initially ?           (Ans-10)
5	SEND                       9567      What is the value of M,O,N,E
MORE                      1085
            MONEY                  10652                            
(ANS—M-1,O-0,N-6,E-5)
6	Three man  A,B,C went in three direction and had stolen a mule , a horse and
a camel they ware caught by C.B.I and arrested . During their interrogation
they gave the following statements.
           A: B had stolen a horse
           B: A and C are both lying and I had stolen nothing.
           C: A is lying and B had stolen a mule
One who had stolen a camel is telling lie and one who had stolen a horse is
telling truth.
Among A,B,C who had stolen which animal ?        
 (Ans- A-camel,B-mule,C-horse)

